      "problem": "What is the value of  $\\displaystyle{\\sum_{n=1}^3 5^n}?$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum takes integer values of $n$ from $1$ to $3.$ So, computing the terms for $n=1,2,3$ and then adding them, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{3}{5}^{n} & ={5}^{1}+{5}^{2}+{5}^{3} \\\\  & =5+25+125 \\\\  & =155.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
